WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.801
Video three. Switch from Tally in one step.

00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:08.284
First, one time in TallyPrime: turn on its XML
port.

00:00:08.214 --> 00:00:11.764
Press F1, then Settings, then Connectivity.

00:00:11.694 --> 00:00:17.044
Set "TallyPrime acts as" to Both. Set the port
to 9000, and press Ctrl+A.

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:21.058
Then close TallyPrime, start it again, and
open your company.

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:26.242
Now open Hisaab. On a new PC, Select Company
shows Switch from Tally.

00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:30.690
It is also in the Import menu. On the Gateway,
press Alt+O.

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:36.223
Press W for Switch from Tally. Hisaab looks
for TallyPrime at once.

00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:40.870
Esc shows the search. Hisaab looked on this PC
and in the office network.

00:00:41.253 --> 00:00:48.602
In this video, a test Tally answers on port
9260. Your TallyPrime uses port 9000.

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:55.116
Enter shows each company that is open in TallyPrime,
with its GSTIN, its dates and its vouchers.

00:00:56.196 --> 00:01:00.345
Hisaab ticks the company. Space ticks or
unticks a company.

00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:03.260
Press Enter, and Enter again for Yes.

00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:10.893
Hisaab copies the masters, then the vouchers.
Esc stops it, and then nothing is saved.

00:01:11.825 --> 00:01:16.642
The result: 60 masters and 12 vouchers, in 51
milliseconds.

00:01:16.572 --> 00:01:21.922
Then Hisaab checks 46 lines against Tally's
own reports. All 46 match.

00:01:22.122 --> 00:01:26.473
Hisaab only reads from Tally. Your Tally data
stays as it is.

00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:31.686
Each company becomes a new company in Hisaab.
TallyPrime can stay on the PC.

00:01:31.886 --> 00:01:36.169
Your company is in Hisaab. The next video
reads the Proof of Match.

